    "difficultyReason": "Part a is the standard task of simplifying both surds (75 = 25×3, 12 = 4×3) and collecting like terms, matching p27-q5. Part b is the harder demand. The student must reverse the simplification and write 3√3 as √27 by moving the 3 back under the root as √9, then read off x. This reframing is signposted by 'hence' and is short. It is above plain collection (p27-q5), but below the multi-term mixed unlike-surd simplifications of p28-q6.",
